<title>USA: NOVA unit files for $300 mln shelf debt.</title>
<headline>NOVA unit files for $300 mln shelf debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nova Chemicals Ltd , a unit of Nova Corp, of Canada, on Friday filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf registration for up to $300 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>The Nova unit said net proceeds will be used to finance its capital expenditure program and working capital requirements, repay bank loans and notes, repay or reduce loans owed to its parent and for other general corprate purposes.</p>
<p>Nova Chemicals is a Calgary, Alberta,-based petrochemical and plastics producer.</p>
